    "title": "Ganado looks to continue district dominance vs Schulenburg on Friday night - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Max Williams- ,\n6 hours ago Ganado looks to continue dominance in district vs Schulenburg We preview Ganado looking to continue their dominance in district vs Schulenburg\nGANADO, Texas- The Ganado Indians have looked every bit like last season’s 2A Division I state champions over the past three weeks, earning dominant wins over Flatonia (49-0), Kenedy (33-27) and Weimar (49-8) last week.\nQuarterback Landyn Arriaga had a huge performance against the Wildcats, accounting for five total touchdowns — four through the air and one on the ground — to lead the Indians to victory.\nTop playmakers Logan Bures at running back and Austen Pena at wide receiver have continued to produce, making big plays across the field for the Ganado offense.\nAs for Schulenburg, the Shorthorns enter at 2-4 on the season with wins over Hallettsville Sacred Heart and Kenedy.\nKickoff is set for 7:30 p.m. at Indian Stadium.",
